From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - accept a NULL source in a software finup of no data

Since commit 9d7a0ab1c753 ("crypto: ahash - Handle partial blocks in
API"), crypto_ahash_final() is a crypto_ahash_finup() of 0 bytes, and
AF_ALG calls it with a NULL source to hash an empty message. On SPU-M,
ahash_finup() takes the software path for AES-XCBC and returns -EINVAL
for a NULL source before it looks at the length. On BCM6755, reading
the digest of an empty message from an AF_ALG xcbc-aes-iproc socket
fails with EINVAL; md5-iproc and sha256-iproc return the right digest.

Drop the check. With no data, sg_nents() and sg_copy_to_buffer() handle
a NULL list, and a NULL source with data still fails because
sg_copy_to_buffer() copies nothing.

Fixes: 9d7a0ab1c753 ("crypto: ahash - Handle partial blocks in API")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2300,12 +2300,7 @@ static int ahash_finup(struct ahash_request *req)
 		 * supported by the hardware, we need to handle it in software
 		 * by calling synchronous hash functions.
 		 */
-		if (req->src) {
-			nents = sg_nents(req->src);
-		} else {
-			ret = -EINVAL;
-			goto ahash_finup_exit;
-		}
+		nents = sg_nents(req->src);
 
 		/* Copy data from req scatterlist to tmp buffer */
 		gfp = (req->base.flags & CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_SLEEP) ?
